## 1.1 Platform Analysis

This is a **Python-based MCP server** (wecom-bot-mcp-server) with the following requirements:
- Python 3.10+
- WeCom Bot Webhook URL

Python is cross-platform and fully supported on Linux. ✅ **This MCP server can be deployed on Linux.**

## 1.2 Deployment Options Extraction

Based on the README, I've identified the following deployment options:

| Option | Description | Category | Status |
|--------|-------------|----------|--------|
| Smithery Installation | `npx -y @smithery/cli install wecom-bot-mcp-server --client claude` | Free-installation | **[PROHIBITED]** (Smithery-related) |
| VSCode Cline Extension | Install via Cline Extension marketplace | Free-installation | **[PROHIBITED]** (Smithery-related) |
| Manual Configuration with uvx | Use `uvx wecom-bot-mcp-server` command with MCP client config | **Free-installation** | ✅ Available |
| Local Development Setup | Clone repo, create venv with uv, install dependencies | Local deployment | ✅ Available |

**Notes:**
- No remote deployment option is provided (no cloud server hosted by developers)
- No Docker deployment option mentioned

## 1.3 Additional Plan

The README provides concrete deployment options, so no additional plan is needed.

